    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This paper first provides a brief assessment of Law’s contribution to the theory of money and banking. It then examines Turgot’s first writing on monetary economics, the ‘Lettre à l’abbé de Cicé’ to trace the origin of Turgot’s strong antipathy to Law and his ideas on monetary theory. From there it outlines the actual monetary environment in which Turgot wrote, one that featured the notaires acting as quasi-bankers and in which a banking system on the British model was absent Against this background Turgot’s powerful contributions on money and capital formation in the Réflexions are analysed.",
